y from because there were also  constitutional alarm bells ringing  particularly amongst  delegates or mps from the free democrat  liberal party who launched proceedings  before the constitutional court on this  that's right now the german federal  constitutional court is actually set to  rule today whether a nighttime curfew  and strict uh limits on social contacts  that were implemented last spring were  in fact unconstitutional how could that  impact the the current fight against the  fourth wave  what will make all the difference  because the constitutional court which  initially initially was thought to way  too late uh to really make a difference  is now um coming right in the midst of  this fourth wave and it will rule on a  whole host of measures also including  school closures but the whole question  of lockdown the emergency brake measures  that are now no longer possible  because the incoming coalition  had  those suspended introduced a new set of  measures a more limited catalogue of  measures now we're talking about fast  massive expansion of those again and  here politicians actively waited until  after this constitutional court ruling  to make sure whatever they launch from  now  will not be contested within the court  within days  now germany um says it wants to  administer 20 million booster shots  before the end of the year is it on  track to do that  yes and no we heard biontech  now pledge to three more  millions of doses that could be  delivered here in germany but as we saw  in the report it's very sketchy in some  places there's no personnel in other  places they're not there's not enough  vaccine and that's also  why a new  new  drive is now being launched within the  incoming chancery which is to be headed  by someone from the military at least  projecting kind of military style  logistics and operation  whether that will translate on the  ground when for instance dentists and  will be asked to join this drive and  that's a big question mark